<BaseLayout title="Privacy | TerribleTurtles" description="How this site handles data.">
  <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="meta-note">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-04">2026-10-04</time></p>

    <h2>What this site does</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a set of static pages. It does not set cookies, run analytics, track visitors,
      or have any forms or accounts. It does not ask for or store personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted by Cloudflare. To deliver and protect the site, Cloudflare processes request
      data such as IP addresses, which it handles under its own{' '}
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If Cloudflare detects suspicious traffic, it may set strictly necessary security cookies to tell
      people apart from automated traffic. Those cookies come from Cloudflare's protection systems, not
      from this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>Links to other sites, such as my projects or GitHub, lead to sites with their own privacy policies.</p>

    <h2>Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control</h2>
    <p>
      This site does not track you, so there is nothing to opt out of. Do Not Track and Global Privacy
      Control signals need no special handling here.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:hello@terribleturtles.dev">hello@terribleturtles.dev</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
